    explanation: "Landed cost is the true, all-in price of getting imported goods from a supplier to your warehouse, and it is almost always higher than the product price alone. This landed cost calculator adds the product cost, freight, applicable duty, and insurance to reveal the real cost per shipment, so you can price your goods for genuine profit rather than a margin that quietly evaporates once import fees arrive.\n\nWhy this matters: many importers set retail prices against the factory quote and are shocked when freight, customs duty, and insurance erode their expected profit. By calculating landed cost up front, you see the complete picture before committing to an order, can compare suppliers on total cost rather than headline price, and can decide whether a shipment is worth importing at all.\n\nThe calculation works because each element is a distinct, unavoidable cost of import, and duty in particular is charged as a percentage of the goods' value, which the calculator applies for you. Sourcing managers, ecommerce sellers, and small importers rely on landed cost to negotiate with suppliers, choose shipping methods, and set prices that survive contact with the real costs of international trade instead of collapsing under hidden fees.",
